<title>UK: B.A.T off on renewed lawsuit worries.</title>
<headline>B.A.T off on renewed lawsuit worries.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in B.A.T Industries fell on Thursday amid fresh concerns about the company's exposure to tobacco lawsuits, dealers said.</p>
<p>By 0923 GMT, B.A.T shares were off 12p at 473-1/2.</p>
<p>The worries were fanned by an ABC news report in the U.S. that Brooke Group chairman Bennett LeBow, whose company owns Liggett Group Inc, is offering U.S. attorneys general 30 years worth of potentially damaging secret documents.</p>
<p>The documents are from the industry's own research and apparently show that tobacco companies long knew smoking was dangerous. They are being offered in return for immunity from government lawsuits against Liggett.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
</text>
